title: Moscow's Verdict
subtitle: The International decides who is to blame for the German October.
new-page: true
tags: rf_event
view-if: year = 1924 and rf_over = 0
max-visits: 1
on-arrival: {!
Q.line = 'bolshevization';
Q.verdict_seen = 1;
var blamed = Q.october_leader || Q.leader;
Q.blamed = blamed;
Q.blamed_name = window.RF.names[blamed];
var hit = Q.october_outcome == 'crushed' ? 35 : 25;
var loss = Q.october_outcome == 'crushed' ? 15 : 10;
Q[blamed + '_moscow'] -= hit;
// Moscow's favourite inherits the blamed faction's following
var target = window.RF.moscowFavourite(Q, blamed);
window.RF.shift(Q, blamed, target, loss);
window.RF.normalize(Q);
!}

= Moscow's Verdict

In January 1924 the Presidium of the International meets on the German question. Zinoviev needs the October defeat to be someone else's fault: his own rivals in Moscow are already using it against him. The verdict is that the German revolution was lost by the opportunism of the party leadership.

The blame falls on the <span class="f-[+ blamed +]">[+ blamed_name +]</span>. [? if october_outcome == "crushed" : The rising was crushed, and the punishment is harsh. ?][? if october_outcome == "retreat" : The retreat at Chemnitz is called a capitulation without a fight. ?]

The <span class="p-comintern">Comintern</span>'s line turns left. The new watchword is "Bolshevization": the national parties are to be rebuilt on the Russian model, under Moscow's discipline.

How does the German party answer?

- @submit
- @defend
- @reject

@submit
title: Accept the verdict and publish a self-criticism.
subtitle: Pleases Moscow, <span class="f-stalin">Thälmann</span> and the <span class="f-left">Left</span>. Angers the blamed faction.
on-arrival: {!
window.RF.obey(Q, 10);
window.RF.lean(Q, {left: 3});
Q[Q.blamed + '_dissent'] += 15;
!}
go-to: caretaker

@defend
title: Defend the old leadership: the plan was Moscow's, not theirs.
subtitle: Pleases the blamed faction and the <span class="f-center">Middle Group</span>. Moscow is displeased.
choose-if: funds >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: A delegation to Moscow needs money the party does not have.
on-arrival: {!
Q.funds -= 1;
window.RF.lean(Q, {center: 3});
Q[Q.blamed + '_dissent'] -= 10;
Q[Q.blamed + '_strength'] += 5;
Q[Q.blamed + '_moscow'] += 8;
Q.moscow_trust -= 6;
!}
go-to: caretaker

@reject
title: Reject Moscow's right to judge the German party.
subtitle: Strongly pleases the <span class="f-ultra">Ultra-Left</span>. Enrages <span class="f-stalin">Thälmann</span>. Moscow will remember.
on-arrival: {!
window.RF.defy(Q, 20);
Q.autonomy += 5;
!}
go-to: caretaker

@caretaker
on-arrival: {!
var RF = window.RF;
RF.normalize(Q);
// Moscow names a caretaker leadership; the Middle Group is the safe choice
var best = null, bestScore = -1;
for (var f of RF.factions) {
    if (f == Q.blamed || Q[f + '_expelled']) { continue; }
    var score = RF.moscowScore(Q, f) + (f == 'center' ? 10 : 0) + Q.moscow_trust / 10;
    if (score > bestScore) { bestScore = score; best = f; }
}
// the leadership only changes at a congress, so Moscow can only name
// its candidate and strengthen it before Frankfurt
Q.caretaker_defied = 0;
if (Q.moscow_trust < 30 && Q.autonomy >= 60) {
    Q.caretaker_defied = 1;
} else if (best != Q.leader) {
    Q[best + '_strength'] += 8;
    Q[best + '_moscow'] += 10;
    Q.congress_challenger = best;
}
Q.moscow_candidate = best;
Q.moscow_candidate_name = RF.names[best];
Q.autonomy -= 8;
RF.normalize(Q);
!}

= Moscow's Candidate

[? if caretaker_defied : Moscow demands a new leadership, but the German party has drifted too far from it to obey. The Central Committee answers that only a party congress can elect the Zentrale. ?][? if caretaker_defied = 0 : The ECCI names its candidate for the next Zentrale: the <span class="f-[+ moscow_candidate +]">[+ moscow_candidate_name +]</span>. Under the statutes only a party congress can elect it. ?] Until the congress meets in Frankfurt in April, the <span class="f-[+ leader +]">[+ leader_name +]</span> stays in office.
